@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:apps.subcomponent.side_navigation-content a ds:Subcomponent;
    ds:name "SideNavigation.Content";
    ds:summary "Side navigation content contains navigation item groups and, optionally, a context switcher. It sits below the header and above the footer (when present), and scrolls when its contents exceed the available height, while the header and footer remain fixed.";
    ds:anatomyDsl "SideNavigation.Content\n├── Context switcher (optional, primary only)\n└── Nav\n    └── Navigation item group (repeatable)\n        ├── Divider (shown before every group except the first)\n        ├── Group header (optional)\n        └── Navigation item (repeatable)\n```\n\n```\n---\n# SideNavigation.Content — the navigation region of a pane.\n#\n# Authored 2026-10-16 from the supplied planning tree ALONE. No\n# implementation was read, so this anatomy carries STRUCTURE ONLY.\n#\n# One Content block serves both panes: the context switcher edge is optional\n# and, per the tree, appears in the primary pane only. \"Nav\" is the\n# navigation landmark itself and is anonymous — no block names it.\nnode:\n  uri: apps.subcomponent.side_navigation-content\n  edges:\n    # Primary pane only.\n    - node:\n        uri: apps.subcomponent.side_navigation-context_switcher\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"0..1\"\n        slotName: context-switcher\n    - node:\n        role: nav\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              uri: apps.subcomponent.side_navigation-item_group\n            relation:\n              cardinality: \"1..*\"\n              slotName: default\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"1\"\n        slotName: default";
    ds:anatomyClassic "";
    ds:usage "";
    ds:guidelines "## Content specification\n\n### Primary navigation\n\nThe content can include the following sub-components:\n\n- Context switcher (optional)\n- Navigation item groups\n\nThe context switcher, when used, is always positioned at the top, before the navigation item groups.\n\n### Secondary navigation\n\nThe content can include navigation item groups only. The context switcher is not supported in secondary navigation.\n\n## Responsive behaviour\n\n### Desktop\n\nThe content is displayed when the primary navigation is expanded and hidden when it is collapsed.\n\n### Mobile\n\nOn mobile, the content is hidden when the navigation menu is closed and displayed when the menu is opened.\n\nThe content follows the mobile navigation behaviour defined in the main Side navigation documentation.\n\n## Interaction\n\n### Scrolling\n\nWhen the navigation content exceeds the available height, it scrolls independently of the fixed header and footer.\n\n### Overflow\n\nOverflow lines appear below the sticky header and above the sticky footer only when there is additional content to scroll in the corresponding direction.\n\nIn secondary navigation, there is no bottom overflow line. The content simply scrolls beyond the bottom of the viewport.\n\n## Accessibility\n\n### Keyboard navigation\n\nInteractive elements within the content should follow a logical, top-to-bottom focus order.\n\nWhen a context switcher is present, it should receive focus before the navigation items.\n\nWhen the content is hidden, its interactive elements must not be reachable through keyboard navigation.\n\n### Scrolling\n\nUsers must be able to access all navigation content using a keyboard, including content that requires scrolling.";
    ds:tier ds:apps;
    ds:parentComponent ds:apps.component.side_navigation.
